From 96e95342587728572a471e750e894f9b6782a116 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel <kernel@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:05:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] ik2 AMD: dense Q8_0 products with x in shared memory
 (IK2_K_DMV, IK2_K_DCOLS, IK2_K_DLG)

All default off; on: the same bits as off (each row's lanes, steps, expression and
wsum as mv_q8p_kernel's AMD path; zeros hidden from the compiler).
- IK2_K_DMV=1|2: mv_q8p / mv_q8p_conv (K 2304/3072) through mv_q8p_lds_kernel:
  x copied once a block into shared memory (lane-contiguous layout), every step of
  a warp's rows asked for at once, weights and scales non-temporal; convs, alts
  (ranges of 16 rows) as before.
- IK2_K_DCOLS=1|8|16|32: mv_q8p_cols (T 2..8) through mv_q8p_cols_lds_kernel:
  chunks of 3 steps of every token's x in shared memory, the next chunk's x and
  weights in flight under this chunk's sums; mv_q8p_cols_alts true on AMD (the
  looped visits' q|k|v|r|gate one launch, not four).
- IK2_K_DLG=1 (with IK2_HIP_LGD): the window's loop gate dots with a D row read
  once for the tokens (loop_gate_dots_toks_amd_kernel, loop_gate_dots_kernel<U>'s
  sums).
- kd_force (tests); test_dense_kd: on vs off bit for bit on Inkling's shapes
  (8576/6528/1024 x 2304, 2304 x 3072, the head 201024 x 2304, odd row counts),
  convs + alts, window alts, loop gates; IK2_TEST_DENSE_ONLY=1.
