@@ -355,6 +355,14 @@ compares the first n windows with the one-token path row for row. `IK2_BLOCK_EXA
 tiles and the window's own attention instead (a few 1e-5 off: greedy answers then differ with drafting on; the
 contributor's figures below were measured that way).
 
+On AMD (gfx11, wave32) three switches, each off by default and the same bits on as off (`tests/ik2_kernels_test.cu`'s
+`test_dense_kd`, `IK2_TEST_DENSE_ONLY=1`), change where the dense Q8_0 products' bytes come from, for K 2304 / 3072:
+`IK2_K_DMV=1` (2: a row a wave) the one-token product with x in shared memory (a wave read x from the caches four
+times its weight bytes) and every step of a wave's rows asked for at once, non-temporally; `IK2_K_DCOLS=1` (8 / 16
+/ 32: rows a block) the window's, a chunk of 3 steps of every token's x in shared memory and the next chunk's weights
